# Line-ending policy.
#
# THE ONE THAT MATTERS: driver/*.inf must never be translated.
#
# A driver package's .cat catalog stores a hash OF THE INF FILE'S BYTES. With
# core.autocrlf=true and no rule here, Git stores the INF with LF and checks it
# out with CRLF — one extra byte per line — so the file on disk no longer hashes
# to what the signed catalog says. pnputil then refuses the whole package with
# "The hash for the file is not present in the specified catalog file. The file
# is likely corrupt or the victim of tampering", and NO CAMERA DRIVER CAN BE
# INSTALLED.
#
# It fails silently and only for NEW installs — an already-bound machine keeps
# working, so it survives testing on the developer's own box. Every CI build,
# which starts from a fresh clone, produces a setup exe that cannot install a
# driver.
#
# `-text` means "never convert, in either direction". Do not remove it, and do
# not hand-edit an INF without regenerating its catalog (driver/generate_driver.ps1).
driver/*.inf -text

# The rest of the driver package is binary: signed catalogs and DER certificates.
driver/*.cat binary
driver/*.cer binary

# Vendored prebuilt libraries and binary assets.
*.lib binary
*.ico binary
*.bin binary
